    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d740">

                <pb facs="1033" n="913" xml:id="pg913"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77/2657: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Harvey</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                            State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-08-24T11:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 24,
                                1922—11 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received August 24—8:44
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>372. Your telegram 246 of August 11, 6 p.m.<anchor n="83" xml:id="d740-f1"/> I am
                    formally advised that His Majesty’s Government concur in the course of action
                    proposed in the memorandum transmitted by your telegram 209 of July 17, 3
                    p.m.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Harvey</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d740-f1" n="83" xml:id="d740-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; see telegram no. 87, Aug. 11, to the Ambassador in Japan, <ref
                        target="#pg910">p. 910</ref>.</p>
            </note>
